  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "ECwwFj64DyfVMe+ODjie1bMGdHY=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:23:22.676Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Odoo integration point is an automated action on write to a costed field, calling Switchboard as the record layer. Choosing a costed field rather than any field is deliberate: it is the class of change where an inaccurate or unattributed history has a monetary consequence the client can already name.\n\nThe demo has two acceptance criteria in the research text, and both are chosen because they sit outside Odoo's own guarantees. First, the user-attributed change history must survive an upgrade \u2014 module upgrades and migrations are the routine event that reshapes Odoo's own tables. Second, it must span a second system that Odoo does not own, which shows the record layer is not just a mirror of one application's data model.\n\nNine Odoo partners carry this demo, spread across CH, BE, AT and DE, several of them multi-site. The priority distribution is the healthiest of any single-product cohort in this slice: one at \"1 \u00b7 start here\", two at \"2 \u00b7 next\", six at \"3 \u00b7 later\" and none marked do-not-pitch. A concrete integration point plus a cohort with no disqualifications is a shorter path to a reference build than most groups in the corpus offer.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (9)\n\n**1 \u00b7 start here**\n- Camptocamp SA (CH Lausanne/Olten/Zurich + FR + DE) \u2014 not on imprint; Claude Philipona + Luc Maurer per management-board page \u00b7 info@camptocamp.com \u00b7 https://camptocamp.com\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- Coop IT Easy (BE) \u2014 not published \u00b7 info@coopiteasy.be \u00b7 https://coopiteasy.be\n- breida software GmbH (AT Voesendorf (Vienna)) \u2014 Johannes W\u00f6lfl, Gesch\u00e4ftsf\u00fchrer \u00b7 office@breida.at \u00b7 https://breida.at\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Acsone (BE Waterloo/Liege + LU) \u2014 https://acsone.eu\n- Dynapps (BE Geel +8) \u2014 https://dynapps.be\n- Intero Technologies GmbH (DE, 9 sites) \u2014 https://intero-technologies.de\n- OBS Solutions GmbH (DE + CH) \u2014 https://odoo-bs.com\n- braintec (CH + DE + AT, 16 sites) \u2014 https://braintec-group.com\n- manaTec GmbH (DE Dresden) \u2014 https://manatec.de\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Odoo automated action calling Switchboard on write to a costed field. Show a user-attributed change history that survives an upgrade, and that spans a second system Odoo does not own.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:23:22.676065Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:23:22.676070Z"
    }
  },
